# Sequences are fetched, not committed -- see data/README.md
data/*.jsonl
# NOT the corpus provenance: it carries the QC rejection counts (how many records
# failed the complete-CDS gate, the ambiguity gate, the start-codon gate) and the
# input digest. Those numbers belong in the methods section, and the corpus
# itself is gitignored above, so this file is the only record of what was built.
data/*.fasta
# EXCEPT the Spinacia oleracea P00875 reference (475 aa, UniProt, fetched
# 2026-08-30). It is not sequence data in the sense above -- it is the fixed
# coordinate system the active-site harness maps every generation onto, and
# without it results/part_a/tables/l1_active_site_*.csv cannot be regenerated
# from a fresh clone. Committing it is what makes those tables reproducible.
!data/spinacia_P00875.fasta

# Run outputs -- deliberately split.
#
# IGNORED: weights, raw logs, convenience symlinks. Large or regenerable, and
# useless in a diff.
results/**/adapter_*.pt
results/**/*.ckpt
results/**/*.log
results/**/stdout.txt
results/**/latest
*.tar.gz
# .tgz too: the harvester writes results/modal_*/out.tgz, which CONTAINS the
# adapter. *.tar.gz alone did not match it, so a `git add -A` after a run would
# have committed the weights the rule above exists to keep out.
*.tgz
#
# TRACKED (do NOT add these): provenance.json, run_summary.json, history.json,
# config.used.yaml, error.txt, generations.csv and the metrics tables. They are
# the analysis record -- small, diff-able, and the only thing linking a result to
# the code and data that produced it. Note data/*.jsonl is ignored above, so the
# input sha256 inside provenance.json is the ONLY anchor from a result back to
# its exact corpus bytes. error.txt is tracked on purpose: three failed B2 runs
# produced four real fixes, and that trail is evidence.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.DS_Store
